  "notes": "{激|はげ}しい is an i-adjective describing extreme intensity, force, or severity.\n\nFORMS:\n- Adverb: {激|はげ}しく (intensely, violently)\n- Noun: {激|はげ}しさ (intensity, severity)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {激|はげ}しい{雨|あめ}: heavy rain\n- {激|はげ}しい{運動|うんどう}: strenuous exercise\n- {激|はげ}しい{競争|きょうそう}: fierce competition\n- {激|はげ}しい{痛|いた}み: severe pain\n- {気性|きしょう}が{激|はげ}しい: to have a violent temper\n\nUSAGE:\nApplies to weather, emotions, physical activity, debates, and personality. Often implies something overwhelming or extreme.\n\nRELATED: {強|つよ}い (strong) is more general; {激|はげ}しい emphasizes violence or extreme force.",
